  "answer": "two independent evaluations.  stage_extra (splice_a.py:481-516) never computes a loss itself: every number it stores comes from evaluate() (splice_a.py:169-182), called at :489 (baseline B), :493 (B<-B) and :497 (B<-A).  evaluate() calls hook_eval(solver) at :172 and then per_item_eval(solver)['flow'] at :174 -- two separate forward passes over the same 16 validation items.  'hook' is :177, 'per_item_mean' is np.mean(per) at :179 over the SECOND pass's values, and the reported difference is np.mean(per) - hook at :180.  No tensor, list or scalar is copied from one path to the other.",
  "why_the_two_paths_use_identical_arithmetic": "hook_eval (diag1_eval_paths.py:151-173) calls solver.test(track_loss=False), and MultiTaskSolver.test (flyvis/solver.py:473-556) collects one .item() per batch into a tuple (:531-536), averages them with np.mean (:542), divides the one-task sum by 1 (:547-548) and returns that (:556).  per_item_eval (diag1_eval_paths.py:176-202) is the same loop, returning the same list.  Both aggregates are therefore np.mean over 16 python floats in float64 -- the same formula, so the only source of a difference is the per-item losses themselves, which differ between forward passes (the night runs and this package run with cudnn.deterministic False, diag1_eval_paths.py:92-93).",
